2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2469) 'Can the lowering reproduce XLA CPU's own order of adding floats, not only the value that order happens to land on?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2469  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2469) 'Eight cases are not bit-equal on the RTX 4090 today: dot_batched, mlp_pre, mlp_f32, reduce_sum_random, mean_last, softmax_f32, rms_norm_f32 and causal_attention. Each stays within the functional bar, a rel-L2 around 1e-7 and at most a few dozen ulp, but none is bit-equal. reduce with add sums in an irregular tree that changes with the shape, and dot_general runs as a fusion whose accumulation tree also depends on the shape; cases with the order written out, or whose partial sums are exact, are already bit-equal, so the gap is the order, not the arithmetic.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2469  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2469) 'Reveal one new shape's tree, add it to the table, confirm that shape's case turns bit-equal, and confirm removing the table brings the old difference back.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2469  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2469) 'StableHLO: match XLA CPU's summation order in reduce and dot_general
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
